-- title:
--   Stalks of the base-changed model at pole-chart points
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, $F$ a field equipped with an $R$-algebra structure, and $j \in F$ with $j \neq 0$; write $A_\infty$ for `chartAlgInf R F j`, the $R$-subalgebra of $F$ consisting of the elements of $F$ integral over the $R$-subalgebra generated by $j^{-1}$, and let $X$ be the two-chart integral model of $(F,j)$ over $R$, the pushout in schemes of the two maps $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the inclusions of the finite and pole chart rings into their common overring, with structure morphism `toBase R F j` $\colon X \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ induced by the two structure maps from $R$. Let $O$ be a commutative $R$-algebra and let $P$ denote the fibre product of `toBase R F j` with $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $R \to O$. Let $x$ be a point of $P$ whose image under the first projection lies in the open image of the whole space under the morphism `ιInf R F j` from $\operatorname{Spec} A_\infty$ to $X$. Then there are a prime $\mathfrak q$ of $A_\infty \otimes_R O$ and an isomorphism $e$ of commutative rings from the stalk of $P$ at $x$ to the localisation of $A_\infty \otimes_R O$ at $\mathfrak q$ such that: for every $o \in O$, $e$ carries the germ at $x$ of the global section of $P$ pulled back along the second projection from the global section of $\operatorname{Spec} O$ corresponding to $o$ to the image of $1 \otimes o$; and for every $a \in A_\infty$, $e$ carries the germ at $x$, on the preimage of the pole-chart open set, of the section pulled back along the first projection from the section over that open set corresponding, under the isomorphism on sections attached to the open immersion `ιInf R F j`, to the global section $a$ of $\operatorname{Spec} A_\infty$, to the image of $a \otimes 1$.
--
--   This identifies the local ring of the base change $X \times_{\operatorname{Spec} R} \operatorname{Spec} O$ at a point of the pole chart as a localisation of $A_\infty \otimes_R O$, compatibly with the two evident families of functions, by combining the fact that the pole chart of the base change is the open immersion obtained by base change from `ιInf R F j` with the description of stalks of affine schemes as localisations. It is used in the computation of valuations at points of the pole chart of models of modular curves, namely in [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_ord_placeOfPoint_sum_smul_ffEquiv_symm_germToFunctionField_app_iotaInf_eq_one_of_mem_preimage_iotaInf`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_ord_placeOfPoint_sum_smul_ffEquiv_symm_germToFunctionField_app_iotaInf_eq_one_of_mem_preimage_iotaInf).
